    "analysis": "A large, continually updated collection of free digital forensics lab exercises for students and faculty, covering Windows, Linux, and mobile/IoT forensics, network forensics, and AI-assisted forensic analysis (LLM-based browser-history profiling, phishing-scenario knowledge graphs). Materials include PowerPoint decks, Jupyter notebooks, real case-study datasets (e.g. NIST Data Leakage), and Kali Linux tooling scripts, funded by DOJ/DHS/NSF grants and tied to a companion textbook and a COMPSAC conference paper. It is aimed at cybersecurity educators and students rather than practitioners building production tooling.",
